sections.body:
The dictionary has three words for barramundi [ref:hershberger1982]:

- **[judi](word:judi)**, marked as the *[Yalanji](word:yalanji)* dialect word, with *[murrabal](word:murrabal)* given as the Nyungkul equivalent;
- **[murrabal](word:murrabal)**, also marked *[Yalanji](word:yalanji)*, but with *[kudi](word:kudi)* given as the Nyungkul equivalent;
- **[kudi](word:kudi)**, 'barramundi', with no dialect marked.

The two cross-references do not agree, so the dictionary cannot settle which dialect owns *[murrabal](word:murrabal)*. Speakers of Yalanji and Kuku Nyungkal are the right people to sort it out. Fish in general is **[kuyu](word:kuyu)**, and a good fisherman is **[mala-kuyu](word:mala-kuyu)** [ref:hershberger1982].
